    {
      "case": "warp8: win is real but narrow (+0.77%)",
      "evidence": "gap +0.0790 nats over Gauss-full",
      "attribution": "The warp DGP is close to Gaussian after standardisation, so the head-room over a Gaussian baseline is intrinsically small. Treat sub-2% gains as fragile to seed and budget."
    },
    {
      "case": "2-D toy suite is non-discriminative (GMM wins there)",
      "evidence": "see README 'Known limitations'; run with --diagnostic-2d to reproduce",
      "attribution": "In 2-D a 16-component full-covariance GMM is near-Bayes-optimal, and on `gmm8` it is literally the generating process, so it cannot be beaten. The performance gate is therefore defined on the d>=3 suite only."
